    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "Passing through Boralesgamuwa? Check the traffic plan\n\nColombo, Aug. 12 (Daily Mirror) - Temporary traffic restrictions will be imposed in the Boralesgamuwa Police Division on August 13, 14 and 15 in connection with the Bellanwila Esala Maha Perahera, police said.\n\nPolice urged motorists and the public to use designated alternative routes during the three procession nights.\n\nThe first restriction will be imposed tomorrow (13) from 7.00 a.m. to around 10.00 a.m. for the Pawada Perahera.\n\nDuring this period, traffic along the 119 Maharagama-Dehiwala bus route between Boralesgamuwa Junction and Bellanthara Junction will be restricted.\n\nVehicles travelling from Maharagama or Piliyandala towards Dehiwala can proceed via Papiliyana Junction, turn left towards Bellanthara through the Spar Roundabout, and continue via Nedimala.\n\nMotorists travelling from Werahera Junction towards Boralesgamuwa and Galle Road can use Gangaramaya Road and proceed via Golumadama Junction.\n\nThe Ranseevali Perahera will be held on August 14 from 8.00 p.m. until approximately 2.00 a.m. on August 15.\n\nTraffic restrictions will again be imposed along the 119 route between Boralesgamuwa and Bellanthara Junctions as the procession travels towards Bellanthara Junction before returning via Somaratne Mawatha and Vihara Mawatha.\n\nVehicles travelling from Dehiwala towards Maharagama can turn left at Bellanthara Junction and proceed to Papiliyana Junction via Route 117 before turning towards Boralesgamuwa Junction.\n\nHeavy vehicles travelling from Maharagama towards Dehiwala can use Papiliyana Junction and Route 117, or travel towards Piliyandala and access Katubedda Road. Light vehicles can use Malani Bulathsinhala Road, Pitawella Road and Kahawita Mawatha to reach Route 117.\n\nThe main Randoli Maha Perahera will take place from 8.00 p.m. on August 15 until approximately 4.00 a.m. on August 16, with wider traffic restrictions in and around Boralesgamuwa, Bellanthara and Nedimala."
