    "chunk_text": "The main Randoli Maha Perahera will take place from 8.00 p.m. on August 15 until approximately 4.00 a.m. on August 16, with wider traffic restrictions in and around Boralesgamuwa, Bellanthara and Nedimala.\n\nDuring the final procession, vehicles travelling from Maharagama and Piliyandala towards Dehiwala can use Kohuwala Junction and the Kohuwala-Kalubowila Road.\n\nVehicles travelling from Mount Lavinia and Ratmalana towards Maharagama can use Attidiya Bakery Junction, Galle Road, Kohuwala and William Grinding Mills.\n\nVehicles travelling from Dehiwala towards Papiliyana can use Andrews Road from Nedimala Junction and proceed towards Kohuwala.\n\nHeavy vehicles travelling from Horana, Piliyandala, Kesbewa and Maharagama towards Galle Road have been advised to use Kohuwala Junction and the Kohuwala-Kalubowila Road.\n\nMeanwhile, heavy vehicles travelling from Colombo towards Galle Road via Papiliyana or Boralesgamuwa Junctions should proceed to Piliyandala Junction, turn right onto Katubedda Road, and access Galle Road via Katubedda Junction."
